## Database

- `DATABASE_URL` in `.env` (copy it from `.env.example`) is the connection string.
{% if db_is_server %}
- The `{{ database }}` server lives in `docker-compose.yml`; start it from inside the
  devcontainer with `docker compose up -d` (it publishes on `127.0.0.1:{{ db_port }}`). The
  `{% if database == 'postgres' %}psycopg{% else %}mysqlclient{% endif %}` driver is in `pyproject.toml`; add your own client or ORM on top.
{% else %}
- A local SQLite file (`db.sqlite3`); there is no service to start.
